            '   All but First:  FDI
            '   ---------------------
            '   General approach (also to Portfolio investment):
            '    1.  Determine global stock amounts of FDI relative to GDP - keeps in reasonable balance and
            '        allows globalization swing scenarios; increase that at slow rate
            '    2.  As move to country level, identify a long-term ratio of FDI stokcs to GDP, different for
            '        inflows and outflows, from cross-secctional estimation; converge very slowly towards it.
            '    3.  On top of convergence process use growth rates.
            '       a.  First, rely on recent past growth rates, but phase out over 10 years
            '       b.  Phase to long-term exogenous growth rates by country over 10 years (xfidstrockr).
            '    4.  Could add responsiveness to exchange rate swings (or, if had monetary side,
            '        to interest rates).

            '   All but First:  Save 2nd year values for FDI growth
            '   ---------------------------------------------------
            'jrs 2014/09/16
            Dim WFDIGR As Single, WGDPGrowth As Single, TbName As String, WLIFEXPComp As Single, WLifExp As Single
            Dim SWifExpGap As Single, WLifExpGap As Single, WLifExpTerm As Single, WFDIR As Single, WFDI As Single, wfdiin As Single, wfdiout As Single

