                        'bbh 2021/09/21 Possible for prices elsewhere to pull exports out of countries also facing shortages
                        '                If SST(R%, S%) / (StBase(R%, S%) * dstl) < 0.5 Then xc(R%, S%) = xc(R%, S%) - 0.2 * (StBase(R%, S%) * dstl - SST(R%, S%))
                        'bbh 2022/10/27 Above was commented out; reactivated concept below with two lines but with slower impact and with focus on getting rid of extra stocks or shortages of them
                        'Stock shortages can exist, e,g. in Sudan services toward 2100, because early surge of ag imports causes debt build up, EXRATE fall, and long export rise
